  41, 42 DA 614
  41–44 DA 614-620
  42 DA 616; Ed 109; GW 467; 2T 198; 3T 398; 6T 103, 310; 9T 55
  42–44 AA 342; CS 178, 294; 1T 177; 5T 733; 9T 224; WM 203
  43, 44 2T 667');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 13, 1, '1. As he went out. [Signs of Christ’s Return, Mark 13:1–37=Matt. 24:1–51=Luke 21:5–38. Major comment: Matthew.]');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 13, 8, '8. Troubles. Textual evidence favors (cf. p. 146) omitting this word.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 13, 9, '9. Take heed. Matthew (ch. 24) omits that part of Jesus’ discourse recorded in Mark 13:9–12, probably for the reason that he had already reported practically the same observations and counsels from an earlier discourse. For comment on these verses see on Matt. 10:17–21.
Councils. Undoubtedly a reference to the local Jewish sanhedrins, or courts, which met in the various synagogues (see p. 56).
Rulers and kings. Primarily a reference to Gentile rulers.
Testimony against them. Preferably, “bear witness before them” (see on Matt. 10:18).');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 13, 10, '10. Published. Gr. kērussō, “to proclaim” or “to herald,” hence, “to preach.”');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 13, 11, '11. Lead you. Meaning here that they would be “led away to court, to a magistrate, or to punishment” (see Matt. 10:18; Luke 21:12; Luke 22:54; Acts 25:17; etc.).
Take no thought. That is, no anxious thought; “do not be anxious” (see on Matt. 6:25; 10:19).
Neither do ye premeditate. See on Matt. 10:19, 20. Textual evidence attests (cf. p. 146) the omission of these words.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 13, 14, '14. Standing where it ought not. Or, “set up where it ought not to be” (RSV).');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 13, 21, '21. Christ. Literally, “the Christ,” that is, the Messiah. The word is here used as a title, not as a personal name (see on Matt. 1:1).');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 13, 24, '24. In those days. Mark is even more definite than Matthew as to the time location of these signs in the heavens (see on Matt. 24:29).');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 13, 25, '25. Shall fall. See on Matt. 24:29. Vincent (Word Studies in the New Testament) calls this “a rendering which falls very far short of the graphic original.” He notes that the Greek stresses the sense of continuousness, as of a shower of falling stars. See on Rev. 6:13.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 13, 34, '34. A far journey. Mark here omits most of that portion of the discourse recorded in Matt. 24:37 to 25:46.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 13, 35, '35. Ye know not. See on Matt. 24:36, 44. This is the reason for being watchful, or alert.
At even. The four terms here used refer to the four watches of the night, according to the Roman system then used in Palestine.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 13, 0, 'ELLEN G. WHITE COMMENTS
