INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 1, '1. After two days. [The Betrayal Plot, Mark 14:1, 2, 10, 11=Matt. 26:1–5, 14–16=Luke 22:1–6=John 12:10, 11. Major comment: Matthew.]');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 3, '3. Being in Bethany. [Simon’s Feast, Mark 14:3–9=Matt. 26:6–13=Luke 7:36–50=John 12:1–9. Major comment: Matthew and Luke.]');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 8, '8. Done what she could. That is, she made the best use of what she had at hand. That is what God expects of everyone, no more and no less.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 11, '11. They were glad. Possibly the offer made by Judas came just at the time when they were ready to give up of immediately putting into effect their plans (see on Matt. 26:15).
Conveniently. See on Matt. 26:5; cf. Mark 14:2.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 12, '12. Killed the passover. [Preparation for the Passover, Mark 14:12–16=Matt. 26:17–19=Luke 22:7–13. Major comment: Matthew.]');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 13, '13. A man. Apparently a servant, not the master of the house (see v. 14). It was unusual for man to carry water in a “pitcher” or earthenware jar; this was usually done by the womenfolk. Men generally transported water in warterskins.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 14, '14. Goodman. Gr. despotēs (see on Luke 2:29).
Guestchamber. Gr. kataluma, a word used in the papyri to describe any lodging place (see on Luke 2:7).');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 15, '15. A large upper room. Gr. anagaion, literally, any room above ground level, hence, a room in the upper part of the house. Compare the Gr. huperōon, which strictly means “upper room” (Acts 1:13; etc.). For a suggested identification of this room see on Matt. 26:18.
Furnished. Literally “spread.” Here, the reference is probably to the arrangement of the couches or cushions in the room (see on ch. 2:15).
Prepared. In anticipation, presumably, of the Passover.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 17, '17. In the evening. [The Celebration of the Passover, Mark 14:17, 18a=Matt. 26:20=Luke 22:14–16. Major comment: Luke.] That is, the evening of “the first day of unleavened bread” (v. 12). For a discussion of the chronology of the Last Supper see Additional Notes on Matt. 26, Note 2.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 18, '18. As they sat. [The Betrayer Revealed, Mark 14:18b–21=Matt. 26:21–25=Luke 22:21–23=John 13:21–30. Major comment: Matthew and John.] Rather, “as they reclined” (see on ch. 2:15).');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 22, '22. As they did eat. [The Lord’s Supper, Mark 14:22–25=Matt. 26:26–29=Luke 22:17–20. Major comment: Matthew.]');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 26, '26. Sung an hymn. [Retirement to Gethsemane, Mark 14:26=Matt. 26:30=Luke 22:39. Major comment: Matthew.]');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 27, '27. Ye shall be offended. [A Warning to Peter and the Ten, Mark 14:27–31=Matt. 26:31–35=Luke 22:31–38. Major comment: Matthew.]
Because of me this night. Textual evidence favors the omission (cf. p. 146) of these words here, but they are will attested in Matt. 26:31.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 30, '30. This day.According to Jewish reckoning the sixth day of the week had already begun, at sunset, and the trial and crucifixion would take place before the following sunset.
Twice. Only Mark notes this detail.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 32, '32. They came. [Gethsemane, Mark 14:32–52=Matt. 26:36–56=Luke 22:40–53=John 18:1–12. Major comment: Matthew.]');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 35, '35. The hour. That is, the events of the hour.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 40, '40. Neither wist they. A detail noted only by Mark. For similar situation, in which the disciples were speechless, see ch. 9:6.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 41, '41. It is enough. In the papyri the Greek word thus translated appears on receipts indicating payment in full (see on Matt. 6:2). Perhaps Jesus here means that the disciples had slept long enough. Or, He may have meant that the discussion of that particular matter was at an end.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 51, '51. A certain young man. This apparently trivial incident does not appear to have any particular connection with the events of the night, yet Inspiration must have had some reason for including it in the narrative. It has been suggested that the author of the Gospel, John Mark (see Acts 12:12), here refers cryptically to his own connection with the arrest of Jesus. This “young man” can hardly have been one of the disciples, for they had all already forsaken Him and fled (Mark 14:50). It should be pointed out, however, that any suggestion regarding the identity of the young man is no more than a conjecture, reasonable though it may appear. Compare John’s studied failure to identify himself by name (John 21:20–24).
The young men. Textual evidence favors (cf. p. 146) the simple reading “they.”');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 52, '52 Naked. Perhaps completely so, or more likely, clad only in his undergarment, or tunic (see on Matt. 5:40; John 21:7).');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 53, '53. Led Jesus away. [Night Trial Before the Sanhedrin, Mark 14:53–72=Matt. 26:57–75=Luke 22:54–65=John 18:25–27. Major comment: Matthew.]');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 54, '54. Fire. Literally, “light.” It was the light of the fire doubtless that revealed Peter.');
INSERT INTO commentaries (author, book, chapter, verse, text) VALUES ('Comentário Bíblico Adventista V', 'Marcos', 14, 61, '61. The Blessed. A designation for the Deity, to avoid use of the sacred name Jehovah, or Yahweh (see Vol. I, pp. 171, 172).');
